WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.910
Jorah Mormont: When the Doom claimed Valyria,
the great freehold fractured into warring

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:09.250
cities and upstart nations ripe for the taking.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:14.420
Out of the east swarmed the Dothraki, the
horselords of the plains who feared only defeat

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:18.840
and dragons, and now the dragons were all
gone.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:25.150
Under the great Khal Temmo, they sacked and
burned every town and city in their path.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:30.330
No army could stand against them, because
the Dothraki do not stand.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:35.660
The horselords do not draw up battle lines
or hide behind shield walls or layer themselves

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.860
in armor.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.300
The Dothraki charge.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.040
Their blades are more scythe than sword, and
better to cull the infantry ranks without

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.940
breaking stride.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:50.650
Even their archers fire from horseback so
that advancing or retreating, the arrows never

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.650
cease.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:57.980
To the Dothraki, a man who does not ride is
no man at all, without honor or pride.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:03.590
When the city of Qohor realized Khal Temmo
was coming, they strengthened their walls,

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:09.240
doubled their own guards and hired two full
companies of sellswords.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:15.030
The Dothraki were used to glorified farmers
with spears; Qohor would show them a proper

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:19.580
army, with armored and mounted cavalry to
match the horde's own.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:25.240
As an afterthought, the city leaders sent
an envoy to Astapor to buy Unsullied.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:31.270
The slavers had always claimed that the Unsullied
were the great Ghiscari legions come again.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:32.590
Few cared.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.950
The dragon-burned ruins of Old Ghis were a
stark reminder that the age of the foot-soldier

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:38.490
was over.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.870
The envoy had his orders, however, and quickly
bought three thousand Unsullied for the long

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:47.630
march back, for Unsullied do not ride.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:51.110
But while they marched, Khal Temmo arrived
at Qohor.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:56.390
I can imagine how pleased the Khal was to
finally face a challenge.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:02:01.280
By the end of the battle, crows and wolves
feasted on what remained of Qohor's heavy

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.420
horse.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.760
All the sellswords had fled.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:10.641
Qohor knew that the Dothraki would very soon
break through the gates to slave and burn

00:02:10.641 --> 00:02:12.950
at their pleasure.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:20.310
Yet the next day Khal Temmo woke to find before
the gates three thousand eunuchs in formation,

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:23.810
armed with only spears, shields and spiked
helms.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:29.170
The Unsullied had slipped past the Khal's
army in the night while the Dothraki feasted.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:33.490
Khal Temmo had many times their number and
could easily have flanked the small forces,

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:39.200
but to the Dothraki, men on foot are made
only to be ridden down.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:44.140
Eighteen times the horselords charged and
eighteen times the Unsullied locked their

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:51.310
shields, lowered their spears and held the
line against twenty thousand Dothraki screamers.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:55.510
When the Khal's archers rained arrows on them,
the Unsullied lifted their shields above their

00:02:55.510 --> 00:03:01.620
heads until the swarm passed; and then they
held the line.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:07.060
In the end, only six hundred Unsullied remained,
but more than twelve thousand Dothraki lay

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:11.640
dead, including Khal Temmo and all of his
sons.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:17.520
The new Khal led the survivors past the city
gates where one by one each man cut off his

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:25.310
braid and threw it down before the feet of
the Unsullied, defeated and shamed forever.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:31.040
Since that day, the Unsullied fill the ranks
of cities and households wealthy enough or

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.660
desperate enough.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:38.420
Sellswords fight for gold, knights for glory
and Dothraki for blood.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:42.480
To a man, the Unsullied fight only to obey.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:47.510
With the right master over them, imagine how
the forces of chaos would break against their

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:49.239
shields.

00:03:49.239 --> 00:03:54.489
The conquerors, the madmen, the usurpers.

00:03:54.489 --> 00:03:59.709
Between the Free Cities and the Bones, between
the Shivering Sea and Slaver's Bay, spreads

00:03:59.709 --> 00:04:01.920
the Dothraki Sea.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.180
Named not for its waters but for how freely
its conquerors roam upon it.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:11.250
A traveler on the Dothraki Sea will find few
villages and no farms.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:16.329
Because the Dothraki view it as a sin to cut
into their Mother Earth with plows and shovels.

00:04:16.329 --> 00:04:20.669
And the Dothraki know only one punishment.

00:04:20.669 --> 00:04:25.169
The closest the Dothraki approach to civilization
is Vaes Dothrak.

00:04:25.169 --> 00:04:28.580
Though to outsiders, it doesn't look like
a city.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:34.860
There are no walls because the Dothraki believe
only cowards hide behind them, instead of

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:37.310
facing an enemy blade in hand.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:41.060
But the Dothraki couldn't do that here either.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:46.020
Within the bounds of the city, no one, not
even the mightiest Khal, may carry a blade,

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:49.189
by order of the priestesses of the Dosh khaleen.

00:04:49.189 --> 00:04:53.479
Not that any enemy would be foolish enough
to attack the sacred city of the Dothraki

00:04:53.479 --> 00:04:55.099
in the first place.

00:04:55.099 --> 00:05:00.469
Two giant bronze stallions rear over the entrance
to the city, their hooves meeting in the air

00:05:00.469 --> 00:05:04.430
to form an arch, the famous Horse Gate.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:09.680
Through it is the Godsway, where the Dothraki
drag the sacred idols of the cities and peoples

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.190
they've broken.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:16.360
Along one side, stone gods look down on you
from cracked thrones with chipped and stained

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:19.860
faces, their names lost to time.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:22.969
Across the road, monsters watch you pass.

00:05:22.969 --> 00:05:28.889
Black iron dragons with jewels for eyes, roaring
griffins, manticores with barbed tails poised

00:05:28.889 --> 00:05:32.830
to strike and other terrible beasts from every
corner of Essos.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:36.050
But there is nothing to fear.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:41.860
If these gods and devils had any power, they
would never have ended here.

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:45.280
Not all foreign gods in Vaes Dothrak are broken.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:50.639
In the Eastern and Western Markets, merchants
worship their god of trade with the sufferance

00:05:50.639 --> 00:05:55.380
of the Dothraki, who themselves don't understand
buying and selling.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:06:01.169
The Western Market is a great square of beaten
earth filled with animal pens, drinking halls

00:06:01.169 --> 00:06:04.379
and a maze of stalls and crooked aisles.

00:06:04.379 --> 00:06:06.720
Even goods from Westeros find their way here.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:11.169
Though the merchants who sell them wouldn't
know a Lannister from a Frey.

00:06:11.169 --> 00:06:15.539
The Eastern Market is, fittingly, a stranger
place.

00:06:15.539 --> 00:06:20.050
The elders of the Dosh khaleen view it with
suspicion and most Dothraki stay away.

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:21.050
They aren't wrong.

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:27.689
The great elephants, the basilisks in silver
cages and the striped black-and-white horses

00:06:27.689 --> 00:06:31.089
of the JogosNhai are harmless enough.

00:06:31.089 --> 00:06:34.889
But I can see how the elders wouldn't want
their younger members to see the warrior maids

00:06:34.889 --> 00:06:39.710
of Hyrkoon, who wear iron rings in their nipples
and rubies in their cheeks.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:44.960
Or listen to the Shadow Men, who cover their
bodies with tattoos and hide their faces behind

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:49.689
masks and whisper dark secrets for a price.

00:06:49.689 --> 00:06:53.210
This is all of Vaes Dothrak that foreigners
ever know.

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:58.449
For only Dothraki are permitted in the inner
city where the Dosh khaleen live out their

00:06:58.449 --> 00:06:59.449
lives.

00:06:59.449 --> 00:07:05.270
A bloodrider, drunk on fermented mare's milk,
once told me that the Dosh khaleen are stewards.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:10.289
They prepare for the day when every rider
of every khalasar shall return to the city.

00:07:10.289 --> 00:07:16.410
And the Dothraki truly will be one blood and
one khalasar again, under the greatest Khal

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:19.490
of all, the Stallion Who Mounts the World.

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:24.479
He will ride to the ends of the earth and
grind nations into dust, and take the whole

00:07:24.479 --> 00:07:26.050
world as his herd.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:29.460
Or so the prophecy goes.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:34.110
Yet the world is vast, with many places a
horse can't go.

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:37.780
The Stallion Who Mounts the World couldn't
rear above a mountain range.

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:40.009
Or leap across the sea.

00:07:40.009 --> 00:07:44.659
Still, the world has been conquered before.

00:07:44.659 --> 00:07:47.520
Just not with stallions.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:50.199
The Doom took Valyria in minutes.

00:07:50.199 --> 00:07:53.129
But the rest of Essos wasn't so lucky.

00:07:53.129 --> 00:07:54.649
Out of the east swarmed the Dothraki.

00:07:54.649 --> 00:07:58.379
And there were no dragons to push them back.

00:07:58.379 --> 00:08:04.039
The Dothraki tide slammed first into the Sarnori,
who called themselves the Tall Men, and whose

00:08:04.039 --> 00:08:08.090
ancient kingdom dominated the grasslands of
Essos.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:13.240
The Tall Men at first scorned the Horselords
as uncivilized barbarians.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:14.309
Which they were.

00:08:14.309 --> 00:08:19.639
But Khal Mengo had united all of them into
one khalasar with one aim.

00:08:19.639 --> 00:08:24.779
To trample the world beneath their hooves
and take other peoples as their herd.

00:08:24.779 --> 00:08:28.110
One by one, the cities of the Tall Men were
overwhelmed.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:32.380
Still, they wouldn't unite against the Dothraki.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:35.580
Many didn't believe the tales of the rare
survivors.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:38.650
No army could move so fast or strike so quickly.

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:43.900
They didn't know that the Dothraki live in
the saddle and have such command over their

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:47.640
horses that they seem to have four legs, not
two.

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:52.100
Where most archers fire from foot, the Dothraki
fire from horseback.

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:55.630
Charging or retreating, it makes no matter;
they are just as deadly.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:09:01.050
But the Dothraki prefer close combat, howling
for blood as they ride down their enemies

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.140
with their arakhs.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:05.060
And there were so many of them.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:10.380
When Khal Mengo's son, Khal Moro, laid waste
to the Waterfall City of Sathar, renaming

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:17.140
it "The Place of Wailing Children," the Tall
Men finally realized their peril.

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:22.340
Led by a High King, they assembled a great
army to break the khals once and for all and

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:27.570
met the Dothraki on what would ever after
be known as the Field of Crows.

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:32.150
The four khals commanded almost 80,000 horsemen
between them.

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:40.500
The Tall Men had 100,000 foot soldiers, 10,000
armored riders, 10,000 light horsemen, and

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:43.280
6,000 scythed chariots.

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:47.880
As battle was joined, the earth-shattering
advance of the Tall Men's chariots smashed

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:51.950
through the center of the Dothraki horde,
the spinning blades on their wheels slicing

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:54.960
through the legs of the Dothraki horses.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:10:00.700
When one khal went down before them, cut to
pieces and trampled, his khalasar broke and

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:01.700
fled.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:05.650
The chariots thundered after the fleeing horsemen,
and the High King and his armored riders plunged

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:10.740
in after them, followed by their foot soldiers,
waving their spears and screaming in victory.

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:13.340
But it was a trap.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:17.460
The Dothraki were not fleeing, as the Tall
Men realized when the Horselords suddenly

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:21.550
turned their horses and unleashed a storm
of arrows.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:26.070
Two more khalasars swept down on the Tall
Men's flanks while another attacked them from

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:28.620
the rear, cutting off their retreat.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:32.770
Completely encircled, the High King and his
mighty host was destroyed.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:35.780
The Tall Men had stood for thousands of years.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:42.240
Now the crows feasted on their corpses, as
the Dothraki squabbled over their valuables.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:47.420
The common wisdom is that the Dothraki tide
finally broke upon the spears of the Unsullied

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:51.510
at Qohor, saving Essos from the Horselords.

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:55.951
In truth, the days when the Dothraki could
threaten the entire world had already passed.

00:10:55.951 --> 00:11:02.490
The great khalasar forged by Khal Mengo had
splintered into a dozen hordes after the death

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:07.120
of the last great khal, and the riders had
resumed their petty feuds.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:13.550
The grasslands of Essos are now called the
Dothraki Sea, but no more nations drown in

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:14.550
it.

00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:20.090
Still, the Dothraki priestesses, the Dosh
khaleen, prophesy that one day the Dothraki

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:25.941
will gather at Vaes Dothrak, their holy capital,
and unite once more under the greatest khal

00:11:25.941 --> 00:11:30.070
of them all, the Stallion Who Mounts the World.

00:11:30.070 --> 00:11:34.930
He will lead their people to the ends of the
earth and grind all nations to dust beneath

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:36.000
them.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:42.280
I knew a khaleesi who the priestesses said
would give birth to this Stallion.

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:43.760
She didn't.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:48.550
No doubt, the Dosh khaleen have made the same
prophecy before and will again.

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:53.700
World conquest is an alluring dream, but few
who dream it ever awake to its reality.

